            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Not directly. A 2003 study found creatine supplementation had no effect on muscle protein synthesis after resistance exercise. Creatine works by increasing phosphocreatine stores, which lets you train harder and accumulate more volume over time. That extra training is what produces the additional muscle and strength seen in long-term studies."
