        <div class="mt-16 bg-gray-900 text-white rounded-2xl p-8">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Muscle protein synthesis responds to three things you control: resistance training, enough total protein, and enough leucine-rich protein at each meal. Whey is the best-studied way to supply that, a dosed-up plant blend is a fine alternative, and creatine is the one add-on with strong long-term evidence.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Skip BCAAs, standalone leucine, glutamine and test boosters if you already eat enough protein. Consider EAAs only for convenience and HMB only in narrow situations. Put the money saved toward a third-party tested protein powder and the food that fills your daily target.
          </p>
